## 17. CODE STYLE

- All async functions use `async/await`. No raw `.then()` chains.
- All DB queries and external calls are wrapped in `try/catch`. Never swallow errors.
- Use the custom error classes from `src/utils/errors.js`. Never `throw new Error(...)` directly.
- Functions are named clearly for what they do: `fetchAndStoreCandles`, `computeHealthFlag`,
  `deduplicateAndGenerate`. No vague names like `process` or `handle`.
- No magic numbers. All thresholds come from `src/config/env.js` or `constants.js`.
- Comments are required for non-obvious financial logic (e.g., why MAX not MIN for SL merge).
- Use `DECIMAL` arithmetic carefully — JavaScript floats. Round with `math.util.js` helpers.

